error[E0277]: `Url` cannot be interpolated into an event-handler attribute (`on*`)
  --> tests/ui/reject_url_elsewhere.rs:16:12
   |
16 |     script(url.clone());
   |     ------ ^^^^^^^^^^^ this value would be run as JavaScript
   |     |
   |     required by a bound introduced by this call
   |
   = help: the trait `ScriptValue` is not implemented for `Url`
   = note: HTML escaping does not make a value safe as code: the browser decodes the attribute before running it
   = note: pass data in a `data-*` attribute and read it from a script, or use a Hemx handle
   = note: code you wrote yourself can be vouched for with `hemplate::TrustedScript::new_unchecked(..)`
note: required by a bound in `script`
  --> tests/ui/reject_url_elsewhere.rs:6:19
   |
 6 | fn script(_: impl ScriptValue) {}
   |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `script`

error[E0277]: `Url` cannot be interpolated into a `style` attribute
  --> tests/ui/reject_url_elsewhere.rs:17:11
   |
17 |     style(url.clone());
   |     ----- ^^^^^^^^^^^ this value would be read as CSS
   |     |
   |     required by a bound introduced by this call
   |
   = help: the trait `StyleValue` is not implemented for `Url`
   = note: a `;` ends the property, so a value can add others such as `background: url(..)` that fetch a URL
   = note: choose among fixed styles with `+class=".."`, or implement `hemplate::StyleValue` for a type that can only build valid values
   = note: or vouch for CSS explicitly with `hemplate::TrustedStyle::new_unchecked(..)`
note: required by a bound in `style`
  --> tests/ui/reject_url_elsewhere.rs:7:18
   |
 7 | fn style(_: impl StyleValue) {}
   |                  ^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `style`

